    "title": "Buyam/Sellam Junior Design Project",
    "description": "I worked with a development team and client to create an application to facilitate trade in rural Cameroon, Africa. This project was spread out over the course of two semesters. The first semester we focused on creating user stories, finding potential issues with our design, and ensuring our app was accessible to our target audience. The second semester was dedicated to coding the application using Android Studio in Java. The client we were working with asked for us to create a mobile app to be used for Cameroonian farmers to trade as there is civil unrest in the region. By moving the browsing and negotiation aspect of trade online, buyers and vendors would spend less time at open air markets where it is potentially unsafe.",
